{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011JUaVbAJRRAoNwUQma2BhL","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"PLAN-185 W0 (4th pass, INVERTED rule) — oracle for the installer write-safety census.\n2\t\n3\tCovers ``.claude/scripts/check-installer-write-safety.py``.\n4\t\n5\tWHAT CHANGED, AND WHY THE TEST FILE CHANGED SHAPE WITH IT\n6\t---------------------------------------------------------\n7\tPasses 1..3 of the instrument credited ``guardado``/``nao-aplicavel`` to every\n8\tform they did not recognise, so each review round found another unrecognised\n9\tform: 8, then 7, then 9, then 10, then 16 findings, all one class — \"a shape\n10\tthe parser does not model comes out safe\".  The 4th pass INVERTS the rule:\n11\tsafety is a theorem provable only by a named form, and everything else is\n12\t``indeterminado``, which blocks.\n13\t\n14\tThat inversion is only real if the test file asserts it in two directions, so\n15\tevery safe form below appears TWICE:\n16\t\n17\t* a POSITIVE CONTROL — the form with its guard intact must come out\n18\t  NON-BLOCKING and carry the form's id, proving the instrument can still say\n19\t  \"safe\" and has not degenerated into a matcher that flags every line;\n20\t* a MUTATION — the same fixture with the guard removed, weakened, or renamed\n21\t  must come out BLOCKING and NAME the planted path.  The mutation reproduces\n22\t  the MECHANISM the prover inspects (the ``-L`` test, the escaping\n23\t  replacement, the dominating scope), never merely its appearance\n24\t  ([[feedback-positive-control-must-reproduce-the-mechanism]]).\n25\t\n26\t``TestRailRegressions`` then replays every open pair-rail finding about this\n27\tinstrument as a fixture.  Each of those forms was classified NON-blocking by\n28\tthe old rule; each must block now.  The mapping from test to finding id is in\n29\tthe docstring of each test and, in full, in\n30\t``.claude/plans/PLAN-185/w0-censo-S329.md`` §5.\n31\t\n32\tHermetic: every mechanism assertion builds its own shell corpus under a\n33\ttempdir and points the census at it with ``--repo-root``.  The live-repo\n34\tassertions are READ-ONLY: this file never executes an installer and never\n35\twrites outside the tempdir.\n36\t\"\"\"\n37\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n38\t\n39\timport json\n40\timport shutil\n41\timport subprocess\n42\timport sys\n43\timport tempfile\n44\timport unittest\n45\tfrom pathlib import Path\n46\tfrom typing import Dict, List, Optional, Sequence, Tuple\n47\t\n48\tREPO = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[3]\n49\tCENSUS = REPO / \".claude\" / \"scripts\" / \"check-installer-write-safety.py\"\n50\tBASELINE = REPO / \".claude\" / \"scripts\" / \"data\" / \"installer-write-safety-baseline.txt\"\n51\t\n52\t# Env isolation is not optional here: every assertion shells out to the census,\n53\t# and a leaked HOME or CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR would let this file read or write\n54\t# state belonging to the real session.\n55\t_HOOKS_DIR = REPO / \".claude\" / \"hooks\"\n56\tif str(_HOOKS_DIR) not in sys.path:\n57\t    sys.path.insert(0, str(_HOOKS_DIR))\n58\tfrom _lib.testing import TestEnvContext  # noqa: E402\n59\t\n60\tBLOCKING = (\"desguardado\", \"indeterminado\")\n61\t\n62\t\n63\t# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n64\t# harness\n65\t# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n66\t\n67\t\n68\tclass Census(object):\n69\t    \"\"\"One census run over a shadow corpus.\"\"\"\n70\t\n71\t    def __init__(self, rc: int, payload: Optional[dict], stdout: str,\n72\t                 stderr: str, root: Path) -> None:\n73\t        self.rc = rc\n74\t        self.payload = payload or {\"sites\": []}\n75\t        self.stdout = stdout\n76\t        self.stderr = stderr\n77\t        self.root = root\n78\t\n79\t    def sites(self, name: Optional[str] = None) -> List[dict]:\n80\t        out = self.payload.get(\"sites\", [])"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dc5b5fe9-2c6b-46ea-80f3-b2c4ce2f3240","uuid":"98de66de-cdf6-4971-b6b8-0b995cd44281","timestamp":"2026-11-13T18:26:08.622Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.nUJTgA/tree/.claude/scripts/tests/test_check_installer_write_safety.py","content":"\"\"\"PLAN-185 W0 (4th pass, INVERTED rule) — oracle for the installer write-safety census.\n\nCovers ``.claude/scripts/check-installer-write-safety.py``.\n\nWHAT CHANGED, AND WHY THE TEST FILE CHANGED SHAPE WITH IT\n---------------------------------------------------------\nPasses 1..3 of the instrument credited ``guardado``/``nao-aplicavel`` to every\nform they did not recognise, so each review round found another unrecognised\nform: 8, then 7, then 9, then 10, then 16 findings, all one class — \"a shape\nthe parser does not model comes out safe\".  The 4th pass INVERTS the rule:\nsafety is a theorem provable only by a named form, and everything else is\n``indeterminado``, which blocks.\n\nThat inversion is only real if the test file asserts it in two directions, so\nevery safe form below appears TWICE:\n\n* a POSITIVE CONTROL — the form with its guard intact must come out\n  NON-BLOCKING and carry the form's id, proving the instrument can still say\n  \"safe\" and has not degenerated into a matcher that flags every line;\n* a MUTATION — the same fixture with the guard removed, weakened, or renamed\n  must come out BLOCKING and NAME the planted path.  The mutation reproduces\n  the MECHANISM the prover inspects (the ``-L`` test, the escaping\n  replacement, the dominating scope), never merely its appearance\n  ([[feedback-positive-control-must-reproduce-the-mechanism]]).\n\n``TestRailRegressions`` then replays every open pair-rail finding about this\ninstrument as a fixture.  Each of those forms was classified NON-blocking by\nthe old rule; each must block now.  The mapping from test to finding id is in\nthe docstring of each test and, in full, in\n``.claude/plans/PLAN-185/w0-censo-S329.md`` §5.\n\nHermetic: every mechanism assertion builds its own shell corpus under a\ntempdir and points the census at it with ``--repo-root``.  The live-repo\nassertions are READ-ONLY: this file never executes an installer and never\nwrites outside the tempdir.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport json\nimport shutil\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nimport unittest\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Dict, List, Optional, Sequence, Tuple\n\nREPO = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[3]\nCENSUS = REPO / \".claude\" / \"scripts\" / \"check-installer-write-safety.py\"\nBASELINE = REPO / \".claude\" / \"scripts\" / \"data\" / \"installer-write-safety-baseline.txt\"\n\n# Env isolation is not optional here: every assertion shells out to the census,\n# and a leaked HOME or CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR would let this file read or write\n# state belonging to the real session.\n_HOOKS_DIR = REPO / \".claude\" / \"hooks\"\nif str(_HOOKS_DIR) not in sys.path:\n    sys.path.insert(0, str(_HOOKS_DIR))\nfrom _lib.testing import TestEnvContext  # noqa: E402\n\nBLOCKING = (\"desguardado\", \"indeterminado\")\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# harness\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\nclass Census(object):\n    \"\"\"One census run over a shadow corpus.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, rc: int, payload: Optional[dict], stdout: str,\n                 stderr: str, root: Path) -> None:\n        self.rc = rc\n        self.payload = payload or {\"sites\": []}\n        self.stdout = stdout\n        self.stderr = stderr\n        self.root = root\n\n    def sites(self, name: Optional[str] = None) -> List[dict]:\n        out = self.payload.get(\"sites\", [])","numLines":80,"startLine":1,"totalLines":2488}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_011JUaVbAJRRAoNwUQma2BhL","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
