{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017cTcetpPk3n62fPTBZXEQB","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t#!/usr/bin/env python3\n2\t\"\"\"check-substrate-watch.py — Claude Code + Agent-SDK substrate drift watch.\n3\t\n4\tPLAN-135 W5 unit o8o11o12 (O12). The heroic manual changelog sweeps (S214,\n5\tS230, and THIS plan's 8-dimension research pass) became a permanent nightly\n6\tinstrument: a small read-only checker that compares the substrate version this\n7\tframework was last RECONCILED against (`.claude/scripts/substrate-watch.json`\n8\t`last_seen`) with the version actually installed locally — and surfaces the\n9\tfetch-the-upstream-changelog step as a PENDING-OWNER recipe (agents stay\n10\tno-network under ADR-136-AMEND-1; the doc fetch costs no model tokens but is\n11\tthe one network action, so it is Owner-run by design).\n12\t\n13\tA newer upstream/installed version is NOT a defect: it is a prompt to re-run\n14\tverify-the-knob-routes before trusting an assumption baked against an older\n15\tsurface (the S217/S228 silent-knob class). Detection only; never a BREAK.\n16\t\n17\tSemantics:\n18\t  - `last_seen.version == \"unknown\"` OR `_meta.source_stale == true`\n19\t      -> status \"stale-ledger\" (advisory): the ledger has never been Owner\n20\t         -refreshed against the live changelog. ONE finding, disposition=defer.\n21\t  - a code-registered probe (selected by the component's `key`, see\n22\t    `_PROBE_ARGV`) resolves an installed version that differs from\n23\t    `last_seen.version` -> status \"drift\": ONE finding per component\n24\t    (disposition=fix-or-defer; claim names old vs installed).\n25\t  - everything matches and the ledger is fresh -> status \"current\".\n26\t\n27\tProbing is OPT-IN (`--probe-installed`): by default the checker does NOT run\n28\tany version command (zero side effects, suitable for the read-only nightly\n29\tagent which then reports the ledger state + recipe). With `--probe-installed`\n30\tit runs each component's CODE-DEFINED read-only version probe — the argv is\n31\thardcoded in `_PROBE_ARGV`, keyed on the component `key`; the ledger can NEVER\n32\tsupply a command (Codex R2 P0) — with a short timeout and fail-soft.\n33\t\n34\tExit codes:\n35\t  0 — report mode (always), or --check with a fresh ledger + no drift,\n36\t      or infra fail-open (missing/corrupt ledger: advisory + exit 0)\n37\t  1 — --check only: ledger stale OR drift detected (a maintenance signal,\n38\t      not infra failure)\n39\t  2 — CLI usage error (argparse)\n40\t\n41\tPLAN-155 Wave 0 (debate A12) extended coverage to the Codex HOST-harness\n42\tsubstrate: the `codex_harness` ledger entry watches the codex-cli release\n43\tfeed AND the developers.openai.com/codex/{hooks,config-reference,rules} doc\n44\tpages; both codex-keyed components now carry a code-defined version probe\n45\t(`codex --version`), and a detected codex drift attaches the code-registered\n46\tfixture re-record runbook (`_DRIFT_RUNBOOKS`): bump the pin via the ADR-111\n47\tceremony FIRST, then re-record the Wave-1 adapter fixtures.\n48\t\n49\tStdlib-only. Python >= 3.9. Read-only (never writes; --refresh only PRINTS\n50\tthe recipe, it does not fetch). Emits NO audit events.\n51\t\"\"\"\n52\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n53\t\n54\timport argparse\n55\timport json\n56\timport os\n57\timport re\n58\timport subprocess  # nosec B404 — read-only version probes, opt-in, fail-soft\n59\timport sys\n60\tfrom typing import Any, Dict, List, Optional, Tuple\n61\t\n62\tSCRIPT_DIR = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))\n63\tHOOKS_DIR = os.path.abspath(os.path.join(SCRIPT_DIR, \"..\", \"hooks\"))\n64\tif HOOKS_DIR not in sys.path:\n65\t    sys.path.insert(0, HOOKS_DIR)\n66\t\n67\tfrom _lib import cli_currency  # noqa: E402\n68\t\n69\tDEFAULT_LEDGER_PATH = os.path.join(SCRIPT_DIR, \"substrate-watch.json\")\n70\t\n71\t_VERSION_RE = re.compile(r\"(\\d+\\.\\d+\\.\\d+(?:[-.][0-9A-Za-z.\\-]+)?)\")\n72\t_PROBE_TIMEOUT_S = 8.0\n73\t\n74\t# Closed registry of version probes (PLAN-135 Codex R1/R2 P0). The full argv for\n75\t# each component — INCLUDING any `-e`/`-c` interpreter payload — is hardcoded HERE,\n76\t# keyed on the component's `key`. The ledger (and `--ledger <file>`) can only\n77\t# SELECT a key; it can NEVER supply the command. This closes the RCE class\n78\t# completely: an allowlist of argv[0] is insufficient because `python3`/`node`/\n79\t# `npx` are themselves arbitrary-code-execution vectors (`python3 -c <evil>`).\n80\t# Unknown key -> no probe. The ledger's descriptive `local_probe` (if present)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dc5b5fe9-2c6b-46ea-80f3-b2c4ce2f3240","uuid":"0d251573-516c-401d-b4e2-3bee92f49f62","timestamp":"2026-11-13T18:27:33.535Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.nUJTgA/tree/.claude/scripts/check-substrate-watch.py","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"check-substrate-watch.py — Claude Code + Agent-SDK substrate drift watch.\n\nPLAN-135 W5 unit o8o11o12 (O12). The heroic manual changelog sweeps (S214,\nS230, and THIS plan's 8-dimension research pass) became a permanent nightly\ninstrument: a small read-only checker that compares the substrate version this\nframework was last RECONCILED against (`.claude/scripts/substrate-watch.json`\n`last_seen`) with the version actually installed locally — and surfaces the\nfetch-the-upstream-changelog step as a PENDING-OWNER recipe (agents stay\nno-network under ADR-136-AMEND-1; the doc fetch costs no model tokens but is\nthe one network action, so it is Owner-run by design).\n\nA newer upstream/installed version is NOT a defect: it is a prompt to re-run\nverify-the-knob-routes before trusting an assumption baked against an older\nsurface (the S217/S228 silent-knob class). Detection only; never a BREAK.\n\nSemantics:\n  - `last_seen.version == \"unknown\"` OR `_meta.source_stale == true`\n      -> status \"stale-ledger\" (advisory): the ledger has never been Owner\n         -refreshed against the live changelog. ONE finding, disposition=defer.\n  - a code-registered probe (selected by the component's `key`, see\n    `_PROBE_ARGV`) resolves an installed version that differs from\n    `last_seen.version` -> status \"drift\": ONE finding per component\n    (disposition=fix-or-defer; claim names old vs installed).\n  - everything matches and the ledger is fresh -> status \"current\".\n\nProbing is OPT-IN (`--probe-installed`): by default the checker does NOT run\nany version command (zero side effects, suitable for the read-only nightly\nagent which then reports the ledger state + recipe). With `--probe-installed`\nit runs each component's CODE-DEFINED read-only version probe — the argv is\nhardcoded in `_PROBE_ARGV`, keyed on the component `key`; the ledger can NEVER\nsupply a command (Codex R2 P0) — with a short timeout and fail-soft.\n\nExit codes:\n  0 — report mode (always), or --check with a fresh ledger + no drift,\n      or infra fail-open (missing/corrupt ledger: advisory + exit 0)\n  1 — --check only: ledger stale OR drift detected (a maintenance signal,\n      not infra failure)\n  2 — CLI usage error (argparse)\n\nPLAN-155 Wave 0 (debate A12) extended coverage to the Codex HOST-harness\nsubstrate: the `codex_harness` ledger entry watches the codex-cli release\nfeed AND the developers.openai.com/codex/{hooks,config-reference,rules} doc\npages; both codex-keyed components now carry a code-defined version probe\n(`codex --version`), and a detected codex drift attaches the code-registered\nfixture re-record runbook (`_DRIFT_RUNBOOKS`): bump the pin via the ADR-111\nceremony FIRST, then re-record the Wave-1 adapter fixtures.\n\nStdlib-only. Python >= 3.9. Read-only (never writes; --refresh only PRINTS\nthe recipe, it does not fetch). Emits NO audit events.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport os\nimport re\nimport subprocess  # nosec B404 — read-only version probes, opt-in, fail-soft\nimport sys\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, List, Optional, Tuple\n\nSCRIPT_DIR = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))\nHOOKS_DIR = os.path.abspath(os.path.join(SCRIPT_DIR, \"..\", \"hooks\"))\nif HOOKS_DIR not in sys.path:\n    sys.path.insert(0, HOOKS_DIR)\n\nfrom _lib import cli_currency  # noqa: E402\n\nDEFAULT_LEDGER_PATH = os.path.join(SCRIPT_DIR, \"substrate-watch.json\")\n\n_VERSION_RE = re.compile(r\"(\\d+\\.\\d+\\.\\d+(?:[-.][0-9A-Za-z.\\-]+)?)\")\n_PROBE_TIMEOUT_S = 8.0\n\n# Closed registry of version probes (PLAN-135 Codex R1/R2 P0). The full argv for\n# each component — INCLUDING any `-e`/`-c` interpreter payload — is hardcoded HERE,\n# keyed on the component's `key`. The ledger (and `--ledger <file>`) can only\n# SELECT a key; it can NEVER supply the command. This closes the RCE class\n# completely: an allowlist of argv[0] is insufficient because `python3`/`node`/\n# `npx` are themselves arbitrary-code-execution vectors (`python3 -c <evil>`).\n# Unknown key -> no probe. The ledger's descriptive `local_probe` (if present)","numLines":80,"startLine":1,"totalLines":359}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_017cTcetpPk3n62fPTBZXEQB","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
